---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectCard from '../../components/ProjectCard.astro';
import { work } from '../../data/work';
---

<Base
  title="Work · Javier Saldana"
  description="Professional platform-infrastructure work: Kubernetes operators, OPA authorization, authentication services, and AI-assisted developer tooling."
>
  <p class="label">Work</p>
  <h1>Professional work</h1>
  <p>
    Four systems, ordered by depth rather than chronology. All of them are shared
    infrastructure at FICO: primitives other engineering teams build on, not
    product features. Each page states what I built personally versus what the
    team built, and walks through the trade-offs behind the design.
  </p>

  <section class="cards" aria-label="Projects">
    {
      work.map((w) => (
        <ProjectCard
          href={`/work/${w.slug}/`}
          title={w.title}
          description={w.description}
          tags={w.tags}
          metric={w.metric}
        />
      ))
    }
  </section>

  <section class="uid" aria-label="UID Generation Service">
    <h2>Also: UID Generation Service</h2>
    <p>
      A stateless gRPC service generating globally unique, time-ordered 128-bit
      identifiers at 10K+ per second per pod, with no database and no coordination
      layer. I led the core implementation. The most interesting part was
      validation: load testing at 1M+ QPS surfaced a clock-skew edge case that
      could have caused ID collisions under clock drift between pods, fixed with a
      monotonic-clock fallback before the service ever reached production.
    </p>
    <p class="tags">java · grpc · distributed-systems · load-testing</p>
  </section>

  <style>
    .cards {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 1rem;
      margin-top: 2rem;
    }
    .uid {
      max-width: var(--measure);
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 0.5rem;
    }
    .uid p {
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }
  </style>
</Base>
